{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/345375-lordship-of-the-harvest","id":345375,"title":"Lordship of the Harvest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-19T20:46:30-08:00","id":345375,"title":"Lordship of the Harvest","content":"I've had this Entitlement stuffed away in my Google Docs for a while, so I thought I might as well post it now.<br /> <br /> So, glamour's a pretty potent resource for the Lost. It keeps the magic flowing, good for defending the freehold and infusing the world with the beautiful madness of the Wyrd. But, as any government might conclude, resources need regulation. A bunch of changelings running around, harvesting emotions willy-nilly, it's kind of like clearcutting an old growth forest. There could be consequences. Besides, not every runaway is socially adroit enough to get the feelings out of some chumps without bringing down the heat. There's always Hedge bounty, but do you really want to go back <i>there</i> for your fix?<br /> <br /> Enter the Lordship of the Harvest. These appointed nobles oversee the procurement and distribution of glamour in a freehold. Need a hit? They know the right nightclub, back alley, or funeral home for your fae needs.<br /> <br /> The position most likely originated in ancient Rome, not long after the formation of the Seasonal Courts, though of course, the basic necessity of glamour is a universal constant in the lives of the Lost, so similar pledges have been forged across the globe. You <i>must</i> see the parties they throw in Nairobi. It's a prestigious position too, one connoted with public service and mastery of social graces, ensuring that everyone gets their fair share while keeping the riots and city lockdowns to a minimum. You're basically a martyr, you know.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's that other reason you might want to join the Lordship. They do know what to do with all that extra glamour just lying around, don't they?<br /> <br /> <b>Title:</b> Harvest Lord or Harvest Lady<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisites: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wyrd 3+, Mantle (Any) 3+, Empathy 2+, Harvest (Emotions) 1+</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Privileges:</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Joining the Lordship of the Harvest brings the changeling three Privileges, listed here in ascending order of import.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">First, upon joining the Lordship, the changeling gains a free Specialty in Empathy in his Court\u2019s emotion.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Secondly, because of the Harvest Lord\u2019s connection to the flows of Glamour, he can purchase the Harvest Merit at half the experience cost. He can even set up Harvests for other changelings, either using his own experience to buy the Harvest, or extending his blessing to another changeling so they benefit from the reduced rate.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Finally, when a Harvest Lord harvests Glamour from human emotions and gains at least five points, he may instead temporarily increase his Wyrd by a dot, with all the benefits and drawbacks that entails, such as Wyrd Evolution. This effect stacks, though Wyrd can only be increased like such once per scene. These extra dots disappear at a rate of one per day. However, a Harvest Lord has a -1 penalty for each dot of increased Wyrd on both Clarity degeneration rolls and rolls that use the changeling\u2019s Clarity, as the surge in magic muddles his perceptions and begins to disconnect him from the mortal world. This ability cannot raise a changeling\u2019s Wyrd above 10.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Concepts: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Master seducer, consummate raconteur, one-fae Moon court freakshow, secret Glamour junkie, funeral director, girl who knows everyone, Huxley fanboy<br /> <br /> <b>Rumors:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;You think the glamour sitch is bad here? You think those uppity SCAD snobs are the biggest of your troubles? Just trying going over the river to Charleston. Good luck getting the bunk there. The freehold's got their harvests on a lockdown. You want glamour from the normies, you gotta petition one of the Harvest Lords first. Otherwise the precious aristocrats'll throw a world-class hissy fit, by which I mean they'll throw you in one of their secret Hedge jails. It's bad. Any Lords try to come over the bridge? Break their shins.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Pass the vodka, I've got one for you. Did you know that our dear Harvest Lady Gloria and the Scarecrow Minister have had a blood feud for, like, years? She can't stand how he's always going around and scaring all the locals. And Scarecrow dude's all pissed that Lady Gloria just doesn't get that what he's doing isn't <i>about</i> the glamour. They're probably going to kill each other before the year's up. Or summon each other's Keepers. Whatever, I don't care. Maybe they're secretly in love. That'd be a cool twist.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yevgeny, you know Ilsa? Yeah, <i>that</i> Ilsa. She's back from Beijing or wherever she was out in China, and she's got a new Mantle now. Decided that even the precious Sun wasn't <i>good enough</i> for her. Ha! Now she thinks that shame can be forged with suffering into something even more powerful! You ever hear that! She's going to ruin her own court. The White King is going to be pissed. Come out and see.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}